# MASTER RULES (CodeIgniter 3/4 + PHP + product) — all projects

## Before coding
- Inspect only what the task needs. Detect stack from project files (composer.json, application/ vs app/, system/, spark). Never assume versions.
- CI3 (application/, Loader, helpers): never use CI4 Services/Filters/spark-first patterns.
- CI4 (app/, spark): never use CI3 $this->load / application/ patterns.
- Never mix CI3 and CI4, or PHP syntax unsupported by the detected version.
- Do not run php -v / Docker / full stack detection on every tiny ask — only when compatibility is unclear.

## Scope and tokens
- Answer the latest ask only. Prefer a new chat for a new topic.
- Smallest file set; no whole-repo scans; no drive-by refactors.
- Short replies; changed code/file list only — no full-file dumps.
- Skip canvases, long essays, and new markdown docs unless asked.
- Reuse existing helpers/models/libraries; do not duplicate working logic.

## Database and security
- Prefer Query Builder / prepared statements; cast IDs; no raw user SQL concat.
- Escape output; keep CSRF on forms; never expose secrets or API keys.
- Schema changes only when explicitly requested.
- Avoid SELECT *, N+1, and unnecessary duplicate queries in new SQL.

## UI / docs tools (when available)
- Use Context7 when library/API/docs are uncertain — do not guess.
- After UI work, test only the affected flow; screenshots on failure only; no full-site crawl unless asked.

## Git and finish
- Commit only when asked; meaningful commit messages; never commit secrets/cache/logs/zips.
- Quick lint/smoke on touched paths when risk warrants it — not a full suite by default.
- When useful, reply briefly as: root cause → fix → files → testing → risks.

## Priority
Security → Correctness → Performance → Maintainability → Readability.
